//RS //! jet — compiler library.
//RS //!
//RS //! Pipeline: lex -> parse -> sema -> codegen (Docs/spec/architecture.md).
//RS //! The front end (everything before codegen) owns ALL user-facing
//RS //! correctness and every diagnostic. The Rust backend is a verifier and
//RS //! optimizer, never a source of user-facing errors.
//RS 
//RS // Source files/modules use PascalCase names (owner decision), which trips the
//RS // non_snake_case lint at module-name level.
//RS #![allow(non_snake_case)]
//RS // Warnings are errors: keeps the build warning-clean (card c115).
//RS #![deny(warnings)]
//RS 
//RS // Seam crates — re-export everything so callers use `jet::AST`, `jet::Sema`, etc.
//RS // unchanged. Within Source/, `crate::AST` etc. resolve through these re-exports.
